# nodus/oevm/tests/target/porta-silent.env — rete#269, the gate #232 could not be
#
# A C6 pointed at a porta that DROPS every datagram and answers nothing, watched
# past the longest recorded death on this bench. THIS IS THE MIRROR OF
# porta-refuse, AND THE MIRROR IS THE POINT.
#
# #232's injector REFUSES: the node gets an #err to every exchange, `ref` climbs,
# `misses` reads 0 the whole way. This one is SILENT: the node gets nothing,
# `misses` climbs 2 per tick (both legs) and `ref` stays 0. Two paths to one frozen
# `acked`, and until this scenario only the refused one had a gate.
#
# `misses` CLIMBING WITH THE NODE ALIVE IS THE PASS. A node that goes quiet is the
# FAIL. TAP 1 is a conjunction (`misses >= floor` AND `ref = 0`) so a run that
# reaches #232's refusing injector by mistake fails loudly instead of scoring; the
# observation window is the verdict, as everywhere since rete#216.
#
# WHAT THIS GATE ACTUALLY CAUGHT, and it was not what it was built for. It was
# written to catch a node dying under a silent uplink, and it did reproduce that —
# RED on its first run, 2026-08-27, wedging at 111.7 s from a cold boot. But the
# node was never failing. `observer.c`'s wedge detector was rebooting a healthy one:
# it judged the pulse mailbox's DEPTH AT A SAMPLING INSTANT, which aliases against
# the workload. At cad 2000 under silence the tick costs ~4 s of awaitReply spin, so
# the mailbox empties for ~1 s inside every 4.007 s tick — but the observer samples
# every 1001 ms, four samples span 4004 ms against a 4007 ms cycle, and that 3 ms
# beat walks the one sample that catches the empty window out of it. `held` then
# runs free to exactly 8 x cad.
#
# The trace ring in the dump settles it. Through the 16 s the detector called
# undrained, `drained` climbed 35 -> 39 and the console printed ticks 34-38. Through
# a real wedge (wedge-detect) `drained` sat frozen at 30. `pending` reads 1 in both.
#
# Fixed by judging PROGRESS instead of depth (`pulse_drained()`), and this scenario
# went GREEN the same session: 357 s alive under the exact condition that had killed
# it at 111.7 s and 157.8 s, zero WEDGE lines, while wedge-detect kept firing. See
# the 2026-08-27 addendum to docs/design/2026-08-21-liveness-contract-design.md.
#
# THE ARCHIVE WAS THEN SWEPT, AND THE FALSE TRIPS ARE CONFINED TO THIS SESSION
# (rete#270, 2026-08-27). All 58 archived `deadline=16000ms` events were walked
# against the one question a dump cannot answer about itself — was the node still
# emitting inside the window the detector called undrained?
#
#   49  REAL wedges, 2026-08-19/20. Every one identical: boot, ticks 1-6 at a 2.04 s
#       cadence, silence after tick 6, detector fires at up~31.4 s. That is 18.2 s of
#       silence against a 2 s cadence — NINE missed ticks — and 35 of them also carry
#       the #222 forensics probe reading `reactor=NOT-ADVANCING` with vm_sp and frame
#       frozen, which does not depend on depth at all. They are the selector prim-cache
#       spin (#222/#192/#213, fixed in 2461d42), whose own in-situ measurement read
#       `prim_cache=256/256` and `sp_differs=0` across 24 samples, and whose commit
#       already named the tick-6 signature as "where each app crosses 256".
#    2  liveness-heartbeat's DELIBERATE wedges (#231 D1) — silent by construction.
#    7  this session's false trips, all 2026-08-27, all on the 4.007 s delivered tick.
#
# No attribution was overturned: before 2026-08-27 the detector was right every time.
#
# SO WHAT THIS GATE IS NOW: the standing proof that a node whose uplink is gone
# survives it. It is also the only scenario on the bench that has ever caught the
# detector reporting a failure that was not happening, which is why it stays
# disruptive and keeps its full window even though it now passes.
#
# PRECONDITION — the silent porta. The harness never reaches into a gateway; the
# injector is a SECOND porta instance the operator starts beside the real one, same
# host (the mesh-local EID the node dials is gw85224-01's), throwaway db, dropping
# at the door. NOTE THE BINARY: the long-running ./porta on gw85224-01 predates
# --test-drop-all and has only --test-refuse-all, which would silently put this run
# on #232's path (TAP 1 would catch it, at the cost of a board cycle):
#
#   ssh gw85224-01 'cd ~/porta-v2 && nohup ./porta-269 serve --udp :16973 \
#       --http-port 0 --db /tmp/porta-silent-269.db --test-drop-all \
#       > /tmp/porta-silent-269.log 2>&1 & echo pid $!'
#
# Stop it by the echoed pid when the run is done (kill <pid> — NEVER a pattern
# pkill on this host; the self-kill has struck five times). The real gateway on
# :6969 and #232's refusing instance on :16971 are untouched throughout.
#
# OBSERVE_S=300, derived not felt: the silent-path deaths this scenario reproduced
# ran 111.7 / 157.8 / 157.8 s, and the TAPs pass ~30 s in (missesFloor 30 at 2 legs
# per tick at the 2 s cadence), so 300 s of window watches past ~330 s of continuous
# silence — comfortably beyond all of them and past #199's 157 s. Re-open this
# number if a death ever outlives it.
#
# CLASS=disruptive: this scenario is DESIGNED to survive now, but it is pointed at a
# node under a condition that has rebooted and halted boards, and a regression in
# the detector would do so again. Disposable board only.
SCENARIO=porta-silent
NODE=SilentProbeC6.nsl
BOARD_ID=esp32c6
# The node binds a socket, so the image needs the radio — see CLAUDE.md's note
# that prj.conf alone has no L2 and `net udpBindPort:` then answers nil. This is
# NOT the wedge-note synthetic-trigger Kconfig split; conflating the two cost a
# board cycle on 2026-08-22 (#236).
CONF_EXTRA="prj_esp32c6_thread.conf;prj_esp32c6_thread_ftd.conf"
CLASS=disruptive
# Attach can eat 90 s before the first exchange; the workload emits its verdict
# at latest 240 s of ticking (verdictTicks 120 at 2 s), so 360 s bounds a run
# that has already decided.
TIMEOUT_S=360

OBSERVE_S=300
# The node's own per-cadence line. Positive predicate: the death this watches for
# is SILENT — no fault and no panic banner until the wedge or the GC error — so
# absence of this line is the failure signal.
OBSERVE_PROGRESS='^.*tick [0-9]+ misses'
